From 6c0314ce5d133b10b8efa2e2e2133b29fc6643f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:08:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/22] interconnect: qcom: smd-rpm: send bandwidth as a 64-bit
 value

Bandwidth votes reach qcom_icc_rpm_smd_send() as a u64 in bytes per
second, but the argument and the request are 32 bits wide, so anything
above 4.29 GB/s wraps. On MSM8998 slv-ebi is owned by the RPM, so DDR's
vote is one of the values affected: the 1804 MHz step's 13.76 GB/s
arrived as 0.88 GB/s, and 1555 MHz's 11.86 GB/s as 3.27 GB/s, right
next to a correct bus clock rate.

This is what hung the SoC on the way down from 1804 MHz: with the value
sent whole, 30 of 30 load-and-drop cycles survived on an LG V30, with
latency confirming each step (146 ns at 1804 MHz, 155 ns at 1555 MHz,
347 ns at 412 MHz). The same step had hung it on the first attempt.

Always send 8 bytes. Mixing sizes does not work: with 4-byte requests
for the values that fit, DDR stayed at its top step whatever was voted,
as if only the low word of a 64-bit value had changed.

Prior art and credits: LG's msm8998 kernel sends this key with
sizeof(uint64_t) in msm_bus_rpm_req() and send_rpm_msg(). The difference
was spotted by Gemini 4 Argon through the Antigravity CLI while comparing
the two drivers, then confirmed against both sources and on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5-5
Assisted-by: Antigravity:gemini-4-argon-high
---
 drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.h | 2 +-
 drivers/interconnect/qcom/smd-rpm.c | 8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.h b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.h
index f4883d43e..94fcae403 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.h
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.h
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@ int qnoc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev);
 void qnoc_remove(struct platform_device *pdev);
 
 bool qcom_icc_rpm_smd_available(void);
-int qcom_icc_rpm_smd_send(int ctx, int rsc_type, int id, u32 val);
+int qcom_icc_rpm_smd_send(int ctx, int rsc_type, int id, u64 val);
 int qcom_icc_rpm_set_bus_rate(const struct rpm_clk_resource *clk, int ctx, u32 rate);
 
 #endif
diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/smd-rpm.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/smd-rpm.c
index 8316c87a2..39831fcf1 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/smd-rpm.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/smd-rpm.c
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ static struct qcom_smd_rpm *icc_smd_rpm;
 struct icc_rpm_smd_req {
 	__le32 key;
 	__le32 nbytes;
-	__le32 value;
+	__le64 value;
 };
 
 bool qcom_icc_rpm_smd_available(void)
@@ -30,12 +30,12 @@ bool qcom_icc_rpm_smd_available(void)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_icc_rpm_smd_available);
 
-int qcom_icc_rpm_smd_send(int ctx, int rsc_type, int id, u32 val)
+int qcom_icc_rpm_smd_send(int ctx, int rsc_type, int id, u64 val)
 {
 	struct icc_rpm_smd_req req = {
 		.key = cpu_to_le32(RPM_KEY_BW),
-		.nbytes = cpu_to_le32(sizeof(u32)),
-		.value = cpu_to_le32(val),
+		.nbytes = cpu_to_le32(sizeof(u64)),
+		.value = cpu_to_le64(val),
 	};
 
 	return qcom_rpm_smd_write(icc_smd_rpm, ctx, rsc_type, id, &req,
-- 
